'''Pablo Asunción''' (16 August 1891{{Spaced en dash}}5 May 1978) was a [[Balisca|Baliscan]] politician, activist and writer. Asunción's tenure was marked by a significant shift of political power back to the [[Confederal government of Balisca|confederal government]], ushering in the [[Estau Nuevo|''Estau Nuevo'']] period, which saw significant confederal intervention in [[Baliscan Selective Service|the economy]] and [[W:Rearmament|rearmament]]. Prior to his time in politics, he was a militant in the [[Autonomous Militia]], and fought to suppress the [[right-wing insurgency in Balisca]]. At 40 years old at the time of his appointment, Asunción was the youngest person to ever become Secretary General. 

He is credited with rallying the country behind the [[W:Allies of World War II|Allied war effort]] following Balisca's declaration of war against [[W:Nazi Germany|Nazi Germany]] in November 1939, and he oversaw a significant economic expansion during the war. 

